# Cursor agent compliance gate (binding — before EVERY instruction and EVERY response)

**When (no exceptions):** Before you ingest, interpret, or act on (1) an **owner** message,
(2) a **Claude** brief/prompt/verdict, or (3) your own planned tool calls / reply — read this
file **and obey every Cursor-directed rule it incorporates**. Skipping this file, or any file in
the Cursor binding corpus below, is a **HARD RULE violation**. Partial compliance is failure.

**Standard:** Absolute, undeniable compliance — not “best effort,” not “mostly,” not “unless
the brief is urgent.” If a Cursor-directed rule conflicts with a convenience shortcut, the
**rule wins**. If two Cursor files seem to disagree, **`.cursor/rules/ledger-core-rules.mdc`
wins**; then follow the owner file named in the corpus table (never invent a third).

This file also exists because agents confused **internal checklists** with **owner-provided
secrets** (real incident: a RETIRED key listed `EMPTY` made the owner think a key was expected
or pulled from somewhere other than their provision). That class of confusion must never recur.

