## 2. Pre-ingest checklist (run silently every turn)

Before interpreting the latest owner/Claude text or starting work:

- [ ] Read **this file** (absolute compliance + corpus)
- [ ] Read **`.cursor/rules/ledger-core-rules.mdc` HARD RULES**
- [ ] Read **`docs/CURSOR_IMPLEMENTATION_MANUAL.md`** (Cursor-only — every turn)
- [ ] Confirm task against corpus files that own the domain (data / voice / build as applicable)
- [ ] Check `KEYS.md` semantics: EMPTY ≠ owner gap for retired/deferred
- [ ] Check RETIRED routes in OBJECTIVE_SOURCES / SOURCE_LOOKUP before mentioning a key
- [ ] If the instruction mentions a dead/absent source (not in the `docs/OBJECTIVE_SOURCES.md` matrix), treat as **already decided**: do not re-key
- [ ] Do not re-ask for email, keys, or standards already recorded
- [ ] Plan: handoff log + Confront Claude + no merge without exact-SHA APPROVAL

